<p>A technical SEO audit covers everything that happens before Google even reads your content — whether your pages can be crawled, indexed, and loaded quickly enough to rank at all. For a small-business site, this is almost always where the real, fixable problems are hiding.</p>

<h2>What's included</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Crawl errors and broken internal links</li>
  <li>Indexing and sitemap issues — pages Google can't find, or shouldn't be finding</li>
  <li>Page speed and Core Web Vitals, on both mobile and desktop</li>
  <li>Mobile usability</li>
  <li>Structured data and schema markup</li>
  <li>Duplicate content and canonical tag issues</li>
</ul>

<p>Every audit ends with the fixes already made where possible, and a clear list of anything that needs a decision from you — not just a problem list handed back with no action taken.</p>
